message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Agentic Reward Engineering for Risk-Sensitive Portfolio Reinforcement Learning"
abstract: >-
  A large language model authors the reward-function code for a fixed Stable-Baselines3
  SAC portfolio agent, and the experiment tests whether feeding its Eureka-style reflection
  loop a multi-level tail-risk signal (CVaR at four levels, left-tail mass and robust skew)
  produces better reward code than feeding it a single scalar performance number, at matched
  compute, against scalar, single-CVaR, placebo and search-baseline controls. The design is
  pre-registered and cryptographically frozen, and the evaluation uses a survivorship-free,
  point-in-time LSEG equity panel with a sealed test period. MSc dissertation, UCL Institute
  of Finance and Technology.
type: software
